searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","doc":"","title":"DevSupport","ref":"DevSupport.html"},{"type":"function","doc":"","title":"DevSupport.drop_database/2","ref":"DevSupport.html#drop_database/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"","title":"DevSupport.get_datastore_options/1","ref":"DevSupport.html#get_datastore_options/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"","title":"DevSupport.load_database/2","ref":"DevSupport.html#load_database/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"","title":"DevSupport.start_dev_environment/1","ref":"DevSupport.html#start_dev_environment/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"","title":"DevSupport.stop_dev_environment/0","ref":"DevSupport.html#stop_dev_environment/0"},{"type":"module","doc":"A framework for user configurable 'list of values' functionality.\n\nList of values can serve two purposes in business systems:\n\n  1. Making selections between optional system behaviors for some given entity\n     or calculation.\n\n  2. Selection of categorization for informational/reporting purposes.\n\nWhen supporting the first purpose such choices benefit from being well defined\nand closely matched to the functional choices available.  The second purpose,\nhowever, is often times better served by a finer grained set of selection values\nwhich are user defined rather than chosen ahead of time by the application\ndeveloper.  This component offers a solution for those cases when these two\nneeds diverge, allowing the system developers to create a well defined list of\nchoices matched to system capabilities while at the same time allowing users to\nestablish a more extensive and nuance set of choices matching their\ninformational needs without have to create duplicative fields for a given master\nor transactional data type.\n\n<!-- MDESC !-->","title":"MscmpSystEnums","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html"},{"type":"module","doc":"Understanding the following concepts is required for effective use of this\nComponent.","title":"Concepts - MscmpSystEnums","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#module-concepts"},{"type":"module","doc":"The Enumeration identifies a specific list of values used in the system as well\nas carrying configuration for the Enum.  Configuration points include\ninformation about if a given Enum was created by the system developers (\"System\nDefined\") or is a custom, user defined Enum and to what extent the Enum is\n\"User Maintainable\".","title":"Enumerations (Enum) - MscmpSystEnums","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#module-enumerations-enum"},{"type":"module","doc":"Enums may optionally have defined \"Functional Types\" which are intended for\ncases where the Enum provides choices between differing system behaviors.  The\nkey idea is that the Functional Types are tightly coupled with the distinct\nbehaviors allowed by the system.  Functional types are then assigned to each of\nthe available list of value options so that when the user selects a value from\nthe list, they are also selecting a Functional Type which the option should\ninvoke.\n\nFor an example of Functional Type purpose, consider a system which enables\ncertain capabilities when a given master record is either \"Active\" or\n\"Inactive\".  \"Active\" and \"Inactive\" would be the Functional Types recognized by\nthe system, but for the users of the application more nuanced categorization may\nbe desireable.  In this example, perhaps the users want to categorize \"Inactive\"\nrecords by inactive for what reason (e.g. \"In Progress\", \"Cancelled\",\n\"Obsolete\").  All of these values are for system behavioral purposes \"Inactive\"\nbut the extended information can help users understand why records have been\nmade \"Inactive\", perhaps establishing a more complex life-cycle of record\nmanagement.\n\nIf Functional Types have been defined for an Enum, each available value defined\nfor the Enum must also be mapped to one of the Enum's Functional Types.","title":"Functional Types - MscmpSystEnums","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#module-functional-types"},{"type":"module","doc":"These are the actual values which, when grouped together, define the available\nvalues in the list of values which the Enum represents.  Enum Items\nestablish the text displayed to the user, whether the Enum Item itself is system\ndefined and/or user maintainable, and, if required by the Enum, what Functional\nType is associated with the Enum Item.\n\nIf a Functional Type assignment is required by the parent Enum, the multiplicity\nof Enum Items to Functional Types is Zero or Many to One.  This means that the\nsystem doesn't require that all defined Functional Types of an Enum be mapped to\nan Enum Item and that many Enum Items can refer to the same Functional Type.\n\nBeing able to assign multiple Enum Items to the same Functional Type allows for\nthe fine grained information capture which might be desired for a particular\nparent record while invoking the same system functionality for multiple options.\n\nNaturally, if a Functional Type has no associated Enum Items defined, that\nfunctionality will be unreachable by users of the application.  This can be a\ndesirable outcome in some business application scenarios.","title":"Enumeration Item (Enum Items) - MscmpSystEnums","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#module-enumeration-item-enum-items"},{"type":"module","doc":"Enums, Functional Types, and Enum Items are persisted in the database so that\nthese configuration are durable.  When the application starts, all of the Enum\ndata is loaded into a GenServer backed ETS table.  Processes will read Enums\ndata directly from the ETS table as needed.  Changes to the Enums are not\ndirectly written to the ETS table, but are processed by the GenServer which\nensures that the changes are updated in the ETS table, but are also persisted to\nthe database.\n\nThis design assumes that Enum data is read often, but changed infrequently.","title":"Technical Implementation - MscmpSystEnums","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#module-technical-implementation"},{"type":"function","doc":"Create a new user defined enumeration, optionally including functional type\nand enumeration item definitions.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.create/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#create/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_params` - a map containing the enumeration field values used in\n    creating the user defined enumerations.  If the enumeration's functional\n    types and enumeration items are known at enumeration creation time,\n    it is recommended to nest values for those records under the\n    `functional_types` and `enum_items` attributes as appropriate.  See the\n    documentation for `t:MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_params/0`,\n    `t:MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_functional_type_params/0`, and\n    `t:MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_item_params/0` for more information about the\n    available and required attributes.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.create/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#create/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> example_enumeration =\n    ...>   %{\n    ...>      internal_name: \"example_create\",\n    ...>      display_name: \"Create Example Enum\",\n    ...>      user_description: \"Demonstrate enumeration creation.\",\n    ...>      functional_types: [\n    ...>        %{\n    ...>          internal_name: \"example_create_functional_type\",\n    ...>          display_name: \"Create Example Enum / Functional Type\",\n    ...>          external_name: \"Functional Type\",\n    ...>          user_description: \"Demonstrate Functional Type Creation\"\n    ...>        }\n    ...>      ],\n    ...>      enum_items: [\n    ...>        %{\n    ...>          internal_name: \"example_create_item\",\n    ...>          display_name: \"Create Example Enum / Enum Item\",\n    ...>          external_name: \"Enum Item\",\n    ...>          user_description: \"Demonstration of enumeration item creation.\",\n    ...>          enum_default: true,\n    ...>          functional_type_default: false,\n    ...>          functional_type_name: \"example_create_functional_type\"\n    ...>        }\n    ...>      ]\n    ...>    }\n    iex> MscmpSystEnums.create(example_enumeration)\n    :ok","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.create/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#create/1-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Deletes a user defined enumeration and its child functional type and\nenumeration item records.\n\nYou cannot delete a system defined enumeration nor can you delete an\nenumeration that has been referenced in other application data records.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.delete/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#delete/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the enumeration which is to be deleted by the function.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.delete/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#delete/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns true if the requested enumeration is system defined, false otherwise.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_syst_defined/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_syst_defined/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the name of the enumeration to test as being system defined.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.get_syst_defined/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_syst_defined/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> MscmpSystEnums.get_syst_defined(\"example_enumeration\")\n    false","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.get_syst_defined/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_syst_defined/1-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns true if the requested enumeration is user maintainable, false\notherwise.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_user_maintainable/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_user_maintainable/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the name of the enumeration to test as being user\n    maintainable.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.get_user_maintainable/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_user_maintainable/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> MscmpSystEnums.get_user_maintainable( \"example_enumeration\")\n    true","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.get_user_maintainable/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_user_maintainable/1-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Retrieves all values associated with the requested enumeration.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_values/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_values/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the name of the enumeration for which to retrieve values.\n\nThe successful return of this function is an instance of the\n`Msdata.SystEnums` struct containing the values requested.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.get_values/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_values/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> MscmpSystEnums.get_values(\"example_enumeration\")","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.get_values/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_values/1-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Retrieves all values for all enumerations.\n\nThis function returns all other enumeration metadata, such as the records' IDs,\ndescriptions, etc.  Also included is association data for the `enum_items`\nfield and the `functional_type` association of each item.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.list_all/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#list_all/0"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> MscmpSystEnums.list_all()","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.list_all/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#list_all/0-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Changes the values of an existing enumeration.\n\nYou can change the following fields using the this function:\n\n  * `internal_name` - Note that you cannot change the internal name of a\n    system defined enumeration.\n\n  * `display_name`\n\n  * `user_description`\n\n  * `default_user_options`\n\nOther fields of the `Msdata.SystEnums` data type may not be\nmodified via this module.  Also note that only the enumeration value itself\ncan be modified.  Changes to functional type or enumeration item records must\nbe addressed individually.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.set_values/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#set_values/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the enumeration which is being modified.\n\n  * `enum_params` - a map of type `t:MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_params/0` which\n    establishes the data values which are to be changed.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.set_values/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#set_values/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Creates a new user defined functional type.\n\nUser defined functional types may only be added to user defined enumerations.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.create_functional_type/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#create_functional_type/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the Enumeration to which the new functional type will be a\n    child.\n\n  * `functional_type_params` - a map of type\n    `t:Types.enum_functional_type_params/0` which establishes\n    the data values for the new functional type.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.create_functional_type/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#create_functional_type/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Deletes a user defined enumeration functional type record.\n\nYou cannot delete a system defined functional type nor can you delete a\nfunctional type which is still referenced by enumeration item records.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.delete_functional_type/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#delete_functional_type/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the enumeration which is is the parent of the functional\n    type to be deleted.\n\n  * `enum_functional_type_name`- the target functional type of the delete\n    operation.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.delete_functional_type/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#delete_functional_type/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns the internal name of the functional type to which the given Enum Item\nrecord belongs.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_functional_type_by_item_id/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_functional_type_by_item_id/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the name of the enumeration to which the Enum Item ID\n  belongs.\n\n  * `enum_item_id` - the record ID of the Enum Item record of interest.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.get_functional_type_by_item_id/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_functional_type_by_item_id/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> example_enum_item = MscmpSystEnums.get_item_by_name(\n    ...>   \"example_enumeration\",\n    ...>   \"example_enum_item_one\")\n    iex> MscmpSystEnums.get_functional_type_by_item_id(\n    ...>   \"example_enumeration\",\n    ...>   example_enum_item.id)\n    \"example_enum_func_type_1\"","title":"Example - MscmpSystEnums.get_functional_type_by_item_id/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_functional_type_by_item_id/2-example"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns the list of Enumeration Functional Types associated with the requested\nenumeration.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.list_functional_types/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#list_functional_types/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the name of the enumeration for which to retrieve the list\n    of enumeration functional types.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.list_functional_types/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#list_functional_types/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Change the values of an existing enumeration functional type record.\n\nThe following fields may be changed using this function:\n\n  * `internal_name` - Note that you cannot change the internal name of a\n    system defined functional type.\n\n  * `display_name`\n\n  * `external_name`\n\n  * `user_description`\n\nOther fields of the Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes data type may\nnot be modified via this module.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.set_functional_type_values/3","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#set_functional_type_values/3"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name`- the enumeration which is parent to the functional type being\n    modified.\n\n  * `functional_type_name` - the specific functional type which will be\n    updated.\n\n  * `functional_type_params` - a map of type\n    `t:MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_functional_type_params/0` which establishes\n    the data values which are to be changed.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.set_functional_type_values/3","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#set_functional_type_values/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Creates a new user defined enumeration item.\n\nUser defined enumeration items may be added to either user defined\nenumerations or system defined enumerations which are also marked user\nmaintainable.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.create_item/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#create_item/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` -the  enumeration to which the new enumeration item will be a\n    child.\n\n  * `enum_item_params` - a map of type\n    `t:MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_item_params/0` which establishes the data\n    values for the new enumeration item.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.create_item/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#create_item/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Deletes a user defined enumeration item record.\n\nYou cannot delete a system defined enumeration item nor can you delete an\nan enumeration item record which has been referenced in application data.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.delete_item/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#delete_item/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the enumeration which is is the parent of the enumeration\n    item to be deleted.\n\n  * `enum_item_name` - the target functional type of the delete operation.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.delete_item/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#delete_item/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Finds the default enumeration item for the requested enumeration or for the\nenumeration functional type.\n\nWhen no qualifying options are specified, this function will return the\nenumeration item record which is marked as being default for the enumeration.\nIf the `functional_type_name` option is used, then the function returns the\nrecord which is marked as default for the functional type.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_default_item/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_default_item/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name`- the name of the enumeration for which to retrieve the default\n    enumeration item.\n\n  * `opts` - a keyword list of optional values.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.get_default_item/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_default_item/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `:functional_type_name` (`t:String.t/0`) - The Internal Name of the Enumeration's Functional Type.","title":"Options - MscmpSystEnums.get_default_item/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_default_item/2-options"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> %Msdata.SystEnumItems{\n    ...>   internal_name: \"example_enum_item_two\"\n    ...> } =\n    ...>   MscmpSystEnums.get_default_item(\"example_enumeration\")\n\n    iex> %Msdata.SystEnumItems{\n    ...>   internal_name: \"example_enum_item_one\"\n    ...> } =\n    ...>   MscmpSystEnums.get_default_item(\n    ...>     \"example_enumeration\",\n    ...>     [functional_type_name: \"example_enum_func_type_1\"]\n    ...>   )","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.get_default_item/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_default_item/2-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns an Enumeration Item record from the named Enumeration as identified by\nits id value.\n\nOther than using a different identifier to locate the enumeration item record,\nthis function behaves the same as `get_enum_by_name/2`.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_item_by_id/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_item_by_id/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the name of the Enumeration that is parent to the target\n  Enumeration Item record.\n\n  * `enum_item_id` - the id value of the Enumeration Item record to return.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.get_item_by_id/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_item_by_id/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns an Enumeration Item record from the named Enumeration as identified by\nits name.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_item_by_name/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_item_by_name/2"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the name of the Enumeration that is parent to the target\n  Enumeration Item record.\n\n  * `enum_item_name` - the name of the Enumeration Item record to return.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.get_item_by_name/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_item_by_name/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> %Msdata.SystEnumItems{\n    ...>   internal_name: \"example_enum_item_one\"\n    ...> } =\n    ...>   MscmpSystEnums.get_item_by_name(\n    ...>     \"example_enumeration\",\n    ...>     \"example_enum_item_one\"\n    ...>   )","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.get_item_by_name/2","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_item_by_name/2-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns the list of Enumeration Items associated with the requested\nenumeration.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.list_items/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#list_items/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name`- the name of the enumeration for which to retrieve the list of\n    enumeration items.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.list_items/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#list_items/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns the list of Enumeration Items associated with the requested\nenumeration sorted by their sort_order value.\n\nIn all other regards this function works the same\n`MscmpSystEnums.list_items/1`.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.list_sorted_items/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#list_sorted_items/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"Change the values of an existing enumeration item record.\n\nThe following fields may be changed using this function:\n\n  * `internal_name` - Note that you cannot change the internal name of a\n    system defined enumeration item.\n\n  * `display_name`\n\n  * `external_name`\n\n  * `user_description`\n\n  * `enum_default`\n\n  * `functional_type_default`\n\n  * `sort_order`\n\n  * `user_options`\n\nOther fields of the Msdata.SystEnumItems data type may not be\nmodified via this module.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.set_item_values/3","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#set_item_values/3"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `enum_name` - the enumeration which is parent to the enumeration item.\n\n  * `enum_item_name` - the specific enumeration item which will be updated.\n\n  * `enum_item_params` - a map of type\n    `t:MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_item_params/0` which establishes the data values\n    which are to be changed.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.set_item_values/3","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#set_item_values/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns a child specification for the Enumerations Service.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.child_spec/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `opts` - A keyword list of options.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.child_spec/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#child_spec/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `:datastore_context_name` (`t:GenServer.name/0` or `nil`) - Specifies the name of the Datastore Context to be used by the Enumerations\n  Service.\n\n* `:debug` (`t:boolean/0`) - If true, the GenServer backing the Service will be started in debug mode.\n\n* `:timeout` (`t:timeout/0`) - Timeout value for the start_link call. The default value is `:infinity`.\n\n* `:hibernate_after` (`t:timeout/0`) - If present, the GenServer process awaits any message for the specified\n  time before hibernating.  The timeout value is expressed in milliseconds.\n\n* `:service_name` (`t:GenServer.name/0` or `nil`) - Required. The name to use for the GenServer backing this specific Service instance.","title":"Options - MscmpSystEnums.child_spec/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#child_spec/1-options"},{"type":"function","doc":"iex> MscmpSystEnums.child_spec(\n    ...>   service_name: MyApp.EnumsService,\n    ...>   datastore_context_name: MyApp.DatastoreContext)\n    %{\n      id: MscmpSystEnums,\n      start:\n        {MscmpSystEnums,\n         :start_link,\n         [[timeout: :infinity, service_name: MyApp.EnumsService, datastore_context_name: MyApp.DatastoreContext]]},\n    }","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.child_spec/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#child_spec/1-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Retrieves the runtime configuration of a previously started Enumerations Service.\n\nSome services need a mechanism to return features such as `:ets` table names\nwhich are set at runtime.  This function provides the mechanism by which such\nruntime configuration can be returned.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_runtime_config/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_runtime_config/0"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns a map containing the runtime configuration of the currently active\nEnumerations Service, or `nil` if no service is currently set.","title":"Returns - MscmpSystEnums.get_runtime_config/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_runtime_config/0-returns"},{"type":"function","doc":"Getting runtime configuration from the current service:\n\n    iex> old_service = MscmpSystEnums.put_service(TestSupport.get_enums_service_name())\n    iex> config = MscmpSystEnums.get_runtime_config()\n    iex> %{enums_table: table_id} = config\n    iex> is_reference(table_id)\n    true\n    iex> MscmpSystEnums.put_service(old_service)\n    iex> :ok\n    :ok","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.get_runtime_config/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_runtime_config/0-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Retrieves the name of the currently set Enumerations Service instance.\n\nSee `put_service/1` for more information about setting an active Enumeration\nService name.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.get_service/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_service/0"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns the name of the currently set Enumerations Service name or `nil` if\nno Enumerations Service name has been set.","title":"Returns - MscmpSystEnums.get_service/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_service/0-returns"},{"type":"function","doc":"Retrieving a specific Enumerations Service name:\n\n    iex> MscmpSystEnums.put_service(:\"MscmpSystEnums.TestSupportService\")\n    ...> MscmpSystEnums.get_service()\n    :\"MscmpSystEnums.TestSupportService\"\n\n  Retrieving a specific Enumerations Service name when no value is currently\n  set for the process:\n\n    iex> MscmpSystEnums.put_service(nil)\n    ...> MscmpSystEnums.get_service()\n    nil","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.get_service/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#get_service/0-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Establishes the currently active Enumerations Service instance for the current\nprocess.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.put_service/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#put_service/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `service_name` - the name under which the Enumerations Service is\n    started and by which it may be referenced.  This is any name that may be\n    used to reference a GenServer process.  Additionally, this value may be\n    set `nil` to clear the currently set Enumerations Service name.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.put_service/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#put_service/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns the name of the previously set Enumerations Service name or `nil` if\nno Enumerations Service name had been previously set.","title":"Returns - MscmpSystEnums.put_service/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#put_service/1-returns"},{"type":"function","doc":"Setting a specific Enumerations Service name:\n\n    iex> MscmpSystEnums.put_service(:\"MscmpSystEnums.TestSupportService\")\n    ...> MscmpSystEnums.get_service()\n    :\"MscmpSystEnums.TestSupportService\"\n\n  Clearing a previously set specific Service Name:\n\n    iex> MscmpSystEnums.put_service(nil)\n    ...> MscmpSystEnums.get_service()\n    nil","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.put_service/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#put_service/1-examples"},{"type":"function","doc":"Starts an instance of the Enumerations Service.\n\nStarting the service establishes the required processes and pre-populates the\nservice cache with data from the database.  Most other functions in this\nmodule require that the service is started prior to use and will fail if the\nservice is not started.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.start_link/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `opts` - Options for the Enumerations Service. See the Options section below\n    for more information.","title":"Parameters - MscmpSystEnums.start_link/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#start_link/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `:datastore_context_name` (`t:GenServer.name/0` or `nil`) - Specifies the name of the Datastore Context to be used by the Enumerations\n  Service.\n\n* `:debug` (`t:boolean/0`) - If true, the GenServer backing the Service will be started in debug mode.\n\n* `:timeout` (`t:timeout/0`) - Timeout value for the start_link call. The default value is `:infinity`.\n\n* `:hibernate_after` (`t:timeout/0`) - If present, the GenServer process awaits any message for the specified\n  time before hibernating.  The timeout value is expressed in milliseconds.\n\n* `:service_name` (`t:GenServer.name/0` or `nil`) - Required. The name to use for the GenServer backing this specific Service instance.","title":"Options - MscmpSystEnums.start_link/1","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#start_link/1-options"},{"type":"function","doc":"Terminates a running instance of the Enums service.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.terminate_service/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#terminate_service/0"},{"type":"function","doc":"> MscmpSystEnums.terminate_service()\n    :ok","title":"Examples - MscmpSystEnums.terminate_service/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.html#terminate_service/0-examples"},{"type":"module","doc":"The data structure defining the functional types associated with a given\nenumeration.\n\nFunctional types allow the application behavior associated with list choices\nto be decoupled from the information conveyance that the same list of choices\nmay be able to provide.  For example, the application may only need to\nrecognize the difference between 'active' and 'inactive' order records as a\nstatus, however a user may want to see some reflection of why an order was\nmade inactive, such as it was cancelled or that it was fulfilled.  In this\ncase would create two entries of functional type inactive, one each for\ncancelled and fulfilled.  Functionally the application will see the same\nvalue, but user reporting can reflect the nuance not needed by the application\nfunctionality.\n\nDefined in `MscmpSystEnums`.","title":"Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes","ref":"Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes.html"},{"type":"type","doc":"","title":"Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes.t/0","ref":"Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","doc":"Produces a changeset used to create or update a Enum Functional Type record.\n\nThe `change_params` argument defines the attributes to be used in maintaining\nan Enum Functional Type record.  Of the allowed fields, the following are\nrequired for creation:\n\n  * `internal_name` - A unique key which is intended for programmatic usage\n    by the application and other applications which make use of the data.\n\n  * `display_name` - A unique key for the purposes of presentation to users\n    in user interfaces, reporting, etc.\n\n  * `external_name` - A non-unique name for the purposes of presentation to\n    users in user interfaces, reporting, etc.\n\n  * `user_description` - A description of the setting including its use cases\n    and any limits or restrictions.","title":"Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes.changeset/3","ref":"Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes.html#changeset/3"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `:min_internal_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of internal_name values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_internal_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of internal_name values. The default value is `64`.\n\n* `:min_display_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of display_name values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_display_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of display_name values. The default value is `64`.\n\n* `:min_external_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of external_name values. The default value is `2`.\n\n* `:max_external_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of external_name values. The default value is `64`.\n\n* `:min_user_description_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of user_description values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_user_description_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of user_description values. The default value is `1000`.","title":"Options - Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes.changeset/3","ref":"Msdata.SystEnumFunctionalTypes.html#changeset/3-options"},{"type":"module","doc":"The data structure defining individual enumerated values.\n\nDefined in `MscmpSystEnums`.","title":"Msdata.SystEnumItems","ref":"Msdata.SystEnumItems.html"},{"type":"type","doc":"","title":"Msdata.SystEnumItems.t/0","ref":"Msdata.SystEnumItems.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","doc":"Produces a changeset used to create or update a Enum Items record.\n\nThe `change_params` argument defines the attributes to be used in maintaining\na Enum Items record.  Of the allowed fields, the following are required for\ncreation:\n\n  * `internal_name` - A unique key which is intended for programmatic usage\n    by the application and other applications which make use of the data.\n\n  * `display_name` - A unique key for the purposes of presentation to users\n    in user interfaces, reporting, etc.\n\n  * `external_name` - A non-unique name for the purposes of presentation to\n    users in user interfaces, reporting, etc.\n\n  * `user_description` - A description of the setting including its use cases\n    and any limits or restrictions.","title":"Msdata.SystEnumItems.changeset/3","ref":"Msdata.SystEnumItems.html#changeset/3"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `:min_internal_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of internal_name values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_internal_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of internal_name values. The default value is `64`.\n\n* `:min_display_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of display_name values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_display_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of display_name values. The default value is `64`.\n\n* `:min_external_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of external_name values. The default value is `2`.\n\n* `:max_external_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of external_name values. The default value is `64`.\n\n* `:min_user_description_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of user_description values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_user_description_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of user_description values. The default value is `1000`.","title":"Options - Msdata.SystEnumItems.changeset/3","ref":"Msdata.SystEnumItems.html#changeset/3-options"},{"type":"module","doc":"The data structure defining available system enumerations (lists of values).\n\nDefined in `MscmpSystEnums`.","title":"Msdata.SystEnums","ref":"Msdata.SystEnums.html"},{"type":"type","doc":"","title":"Msdata.SystEnums.t/0","ref":"Msdata.SystEnums.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","doc":"Produces a changeset used to create or update a Enumeration record.\n\nThe `change_params` argument defines the attributes to be used in maintaining\nan Enumerations record.  Of the allowed fields, the following are required for\ncreation:\n\n  * `internal_name` - A unique key which is intended for programmatic usage\n    by the application and other applications which make use of the data.\n\n  * `display_name` - A unique key for the purposes of presentation to users\n    in user interfaces, reporting, etc.\n\n  * `user_description` - A description of the setting including its use cases\n    and any limits or restrictions.","title":"Msdata.SystEnums.changeset/3","ref":"Msdata.SystEnums.html#changeset/3"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `:min_internal_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of internal_name values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_internal_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of internal_name values. The default value is `64`.\n\n* `:min_display_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of display_name values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_display_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of display_name values. The default value is `64`.\n\n* `:min_user_description_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of user_description values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_user_description_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of user_description values. The default value is `1000`.","title":"Options - Msdata.SystEnums.changeset/3","ref":"Msdata.SystEnums.html#changeset/3-options"},{"type":"module","doc":"Types used by the Enums service module.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html"},{"type":"type","doc":"Identification of each unique Enum Functional Type that can be associated with\nan Enum.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_functional_type_name/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html#t:enum_functional_type_name/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"A map definition describing what specific key/value pairs are available for\npassing as SystEnumFunctionalTypes changeset parameters.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_functional_type_params/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html#t:enum_functional_type_params/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"Record ID type for the Enum Item record.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_item_id/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html#t:enum_item_id/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"Identification of each unique Enum Value that can be associated with an Enum.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_item_name/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html#t:enum_item_name/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"A map definition describing what specific key/value pairs are available for\npassing as SystEnumItems changeset parameters.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_item_params/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html#t:enum_item_params/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"Identification of each unique Enum managed by the Enums Service instance.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_name/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html#t:enum_name/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"A map definition describing what specific key/value pairs are available for\npassing as SystEnums changeset parameters.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.enum_params/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html#t:enum_params/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"The valid forms of service name acceptable to identify the Enumerations\nservice.\n\nWhen the service name is an atom, it is assumed to be a registered name using\nthe default Elixir name registration process.  When the service name is a\nString, you must also identify a valid registry with which the name will be\nregistered.  Finally, if the value is `nil`, the service will be started\nwithout a name and you are responsible for using the returned PID for later\naccesses of the service.","title":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.service_name/0","ref":"MscmpSystEnums.Types.html#t:service_name/0"},{"type":"exception","doc":"Defines an `Mserror` compliant error module for the MscmpSystEnums component.\n\nFor more see the `MscmpSystError` Component documentation.","title":"Mserror.EnumsError","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html"},{"type":"type","doc":"Represents the available Kinds of error allowed by this Error type.","title":"Mserror.EnumsError.kinds/0","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#t:kinds/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"* `:service_management` - Failure operating on an Enums service.\n  * `:enum_data` - Failure operating on Enums data.\n  * `:enum_functional_type_data` - Failure operating on Enums functional type data.\n  * `:enum_item_data` - Failure operating on Enums item data.","title":"Available Kinds - Mserror.EnumsError.kinds/0","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#t:kinds/0-available-kinds"},{"type":"type","doc":"Describes the structure of an error of generated by this exception.\n\nThe `cause` attribute allows for errors to be nested.","title":"Mserror.EnumsError.t/0","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"type","doc":"The following attributes are those which are set or modified by the\nuser when working with errors.\n\n  * `kind` - The kind of error, see `t:kinds/0` for the available Kinds.\n\n  * `message` - A string describing the error.\n\n  * `context` - contextual information for better understanding the\n    error.  If provided, the context should be of type\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.Context.t/0`.\n\n  * `cause` - The cause of the error, which can be an exception, an error tuple,\n    or any other term.","title":"Attributes - Mserror.EnumsError.t/0","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#t:t/0-attributes"},{"type":"type","doc":"These attributes have their values set at compile time and are used\ninternally by the MscmpSystError framework.  They are not to be altered\nby user code.  Reading these attributes in user code is safe, however.\n\n  * `__mserror__` - Always true, indicates that this error is compatible\n    with the MscmpSystError framework.\n\n  * `__mscomponent__` - The component that generated the error.","title":"Internal Attributes - Mserror.EnumsError.t/0","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#t:t/0-internal-attributes"},{"type":"function","doc":"Creates a new error struct with the given kind, message, and options.","title":"Mserror.EnumsError.new/3","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#new/3"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `kind` - The kind of error, see `t:kinds/0` for the available Kinds.\n\n  * `message` - A string describing the error.\n\n  * `opts` - A keyword list of additional options.","title":"Parameters - Mserror.EnumsError.new/3","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#new/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","doc":"* `:context` - contextual information for better understanding the\n    error.  If provided, the context should be of type\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.Context.t/0`.\n\n  * `:cause` - The cause of the error, which can be an exception, an error tuple,\n    or any other term.\n\n  * `:parse_error` - An error result conforming with\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.parsable_error/0` to be parsed overriding\n    certain attributes of the exception struct.  When provided the\n    `message` parameter is treated as a default message which can be\n    overridden by a message supplied by the error result provided to this\n    option.  The `cause` attribute of the exception struct will be set to\n    a value derived from this option's value, ignoring the `:cause`\n    option if provided; typically you would not provide both\n    `:parse_error` and `:cause` in the same call to `new/3`.","title":"Options - Mserror.EnumsError.new/3","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#new/3-options"},{"type":"function","doc":"Returns a struct of this error type with the error details.","title":"Returns - Mserror.EnumsError.new/3","ref":"Mserror.EnumsError.html#new/3-returns"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.38.4"}}